; Baseline test for --external-directive: register top-level directives that
; ledger does not natively understand, so the parser skips them instead of
; reporting an error.  In "line" mode only the directive's header line is
; consumed. The surrounding transactions parse normally.
newdirective experiment tag=cool region=us
myplugin plugin foo

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Checking    $100.00
    Equity:Opening

; One comma-separated option registers both names at once.
test --external-directive newdirective:line,myplugin:line reg
24-Jan-01 Opening               Assets:Checking             $100.00      $100.00
                                Equity:Opening             $-100.00            0
end test

; Without the registration the same journal reports both unrecognized lines,
; so the option only affects the names it registers.
test reg -> 2
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 5:
Error: Unrecognized source line 'newdirective experiment tag=cool region=us'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 6:
Error: Unrecognized source line 'myplugin plugin foo'
end test
